Third-party software
--------------------
HLA typing (include/singlet/pipeline/hla_typing.h) runs T1K (Song, Li et al., Genome Research 2023,
github.com/mourisl/T1K), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 Li Song, Bo Li, Heng Li. T1K's extractor and genotyper (allele scoring, the EM
over alleles, the filtering of ambiguous reads) decide every genotype; Singlet adds a read prefilter in front of them
and, with the frequency prior, a restricted copy of T1K's IPD-IMGT/HLA index. IPD-IMGT/HLA data: Barker et al.,
Nucleic Acids Research 2023, CC BY-ND 4.0.

data/fusion/arriba/LICENSE: the chimeric table applies Arriba's blacklist (blacklist_hg38_GRCh38_v2.5.1.tsv.gz, fetched by
scripts/fetch_arriba_blacklist.sh, not stored in git). Arriba and its database files are MIT-licensed, copyright Deutsches
Krebsforschungszentrum and Sebastian Uhrig. Uhrig S et al., Genome Research 31:448-460 (2021), doi:10.1101/gr.257246.119.

Third-party code
----------------
src/star/ is STAR 2.7.11b by Alexander Dobin (https://github.com/alexdobin/STAR), MIT license: src/star/LICENSE.STAR.
The pileup's STARsolo Gene rules are ports of STAR's own logic and carry the same license and credit:
include/singlet/pileup/tx_compat.h (intron rule 16384) ports alignToTranscript's concordance test from
src/star/Transcriptome_classifyAlign.cpp, and intron rule 32768 (kStarGene, pileup_engine.h and the GPU pileup's
k_annotate / k_resolve) ports Transcriptome::classifyAlign's per-read gene set with SoloReadFeature::record's
one-gene rule (src/star/SoloReadFeature_record.cpp).

Protocol detection (include/singlet/fq/protocol.h, route_evidence and the single-cell checks of the barcode read) follows the design of
preflightx (github.com/saketlab/preflightx), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Saket Choudhary: a read pair is called single-cell
when the first bases of the barcode read repeat across reads, which random or genomic sequence does not, and assays are named from
their read geometry. The engine's checks are written in C++ and tuned on the libraries of bench/protocol_detect; no preflightx source
is copied. The license text of preflightx follows.

